      "content": "TL 0506 2/68 20.12.67 SAINT JOHN'S ROAD (North Side) Pump and Lamp post facing Boxmoor Hall (formerly listed under \"General\") II Bears inscription: \"Erected for the Public Benefit October 1835 to commemorate the third centenary of the first printing of the English Bible\", followed by quotation. Panelled and ornamented cast-iron obelisk, with later shell pattern water basin. Surmounted by four upstanding openwork consoles to ladderbar carrying hexagonal tapered lantern with finial.  Cast by Joseph Cranston of Hemel Hempstead. Listing NGR: TL0530806190"
